WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.798 --> 00:00:01.810
- [Reporter] Are you gonna appeal?

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.430
- [Narrator] In January, Theranos founder,

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.310
Elizabeth Holmes was convicted
on four fraud charges

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.260
in her highly publicized criminal trial.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.730
Now Holmes' former top deputy,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.390
and ex-boyfriend, Ramesh Sunny Balwani,

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.620
is about to go on trial
for similar charges

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.790
of defrauding investors

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:21.410
and patients about the startup's
blood testing capabilities.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.520
Balwani has pleaded not guilty.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.560
- He's a really important
supporting character

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.470
in the tale of Theranos.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:33.570
He was the person closest
to Elizabeth Holmes,

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.920
the star of Theranos

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.430
for the entire time that
she ran the company.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.263
- [Narrator] Prosecutors say

00:00:39.263 --> 00:00:41.210
that Theranos' blood testing technology

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.470
didn't work as promised

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.040
and that Holmes and Balwani lied

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.310
to attract more investments

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.300
as the company ran out of cash.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.710
As the trial gets under way,

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.090
here's an overview of
Balwani's alleged role

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.080
at Theranos, and a look at what's to come

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.613
in his criminal fraud trial.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.010
Balwani faces federal
charges nearly identical

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.180
to those in Elizabeth Holmes' case.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.680
Two counts of conspiracy
to commit wire fraud

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.970
and 10 counts of wire fraud.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.770
- In the end, one of those charges

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:09.260
was dropped against Elizabeth Holmes

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.240
due to an error by the prosecution.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.740
It was a charge related to a patient

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.440
that had taken a Theranos test.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.710
Although Mr. Balwani and his team

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.080
are fighting to get that
charge dropped as well.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.070
- [Narrator] Balwani met Holmes

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.200
when she was a teenager

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.580
and jointly ran Theranos with her

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.340
as chief operating officer.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.160
Holmes and Balwani were also
in a romantic relationship

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.760
that spanned more than a decade,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.690
growing and fading alongside the rise

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.420
and fall of Theranos.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.080
Former employees said Balwani
enforced a corporate culture

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.130
of secrecy and fear

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.340
until his departure in the spring of 2016.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.970
- He was not the ultimate
decision maker as she was

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.290
but he was the chief operating officer

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.820
and he oversaw the lab.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.930
So he had tremendous influence

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.860
and tremendous power at Theranos.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.300
- [Narrator] Through
witnesses and evidence,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.200
the prosecution and defense portrayed him

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.670
as a complicated figure

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.560
who both contributed to and tried

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.750
to remedy problems at Theranos.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.770
- So we have a really
conflicting picture I think

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:03.830
from Ms. Holmes' trial

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:06.470
about how much Mr. Balwani
may have contributed

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.440
to the many problems at that lab

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.720
because of his leadership

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.740
and also how much he tried

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.000
to perhaps fix some of the problems.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.350
And I think it'll be really interesting

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.000
to see the extent to
which that is cleared up

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.950
in Mr. Balwani's trial.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.390
- [Narrator] Holmes testified that Balwani

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.140
was in charge of the lab operations

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.590
and financial projections
shared with investors

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.200
as president and chief operating officer.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.870
The defense argued that Holmes believed

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.700
she was telling the truth about Theranos

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.310
because she relied on Balwani
for accurate information

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.250
about the company's operations.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.920
- So there was a lot of testimony to show

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.630
that the lab had a lot of problems

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.500
and a lot of those problems seemed

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.890
to be traced back to Mr. Balwani.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.880
We also saw text messages and emails

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.590
and other pieces of evidence

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.020
that suggested that he was very
passionate about the company

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.170
and really did take efforts at times

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.550
to try to remedy the problems.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.680
- [Narrator] The prosecution
also called several witnesses

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.800
who revealed how Balwani
treated Theranos employees.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.940
Former lab worker Erika Cheung testified

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.540
that Balwani rebuffed her attempts

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.330
to raised concerns about
Theranos' technology.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.660
- From the witnesses
called by the prosecution,

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.103
specifically former employees of Theranos,

00:03:16.103 --> 00:03:18.100
I think we got a consistent picture

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.060
that Mr. Balwani is not a nice guy.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.380
He's a guy with a short
temper, a short fuse.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.080
He could be really hard on employees.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.310
He challenged people such
as a former lab worker,

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.000
Erika Cheung, about why
she was raising questions

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.500
about lab practices.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.680
- [Narrator] The defense and prosecution

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.550
also showed hundreds of text messages

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.620
that offered a glimpse
into Balwani's romantic

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.780
and business relationship with Holmes.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:44.100
- They show really the complexity

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.620
of their personal relationship

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.360
and also how intertwined their
personal relationship was

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.840
with their business one.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.970
And the messages also show importantly

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.150
the influence Mr. Balwani tried to have

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.280
over how Ms. Holmes ran the business.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.660
In many cases, it's
trying to correct things

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.730
that are wrong with the company.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.530
For instance, saying
we need FDA clearance.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.430
- [Narrator] That 2015
text message referred

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.500
to clearance from the Food
and Drug Administration,

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.190
which would declare the
company's signature Nanotainers

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.640
to collect finger-pricked blood

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.760
an uncleared medical device.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.880
In a separate message, he
said that company's lab

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.510
was a disaster zone.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.900
- And the prosecution was able

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.830
to use those text messages at times

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.520
to show that there were
problems at this company

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.950
that Elizabeth knew about,

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.450
that she was informed of.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.680
- [Narrator] A pivotal moment
in Holmes' testimony came

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.970
when she accused Balwani of
emotional and sexual abuse.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.080
She claimed Balwani controlled all aspects

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.800
of her life, including how
much she should eat and sleep

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.060
and when she could see family and friends.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.220
A lawyer for Balwani denied
the abuse allegations.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.570
- At the end of the day,

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.010
she said in her testimony

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:54.680
that well, she blamed
him for exerting control

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.440
over aspects of her life.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.950
Elizabeth testified that Mr. Balwani

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.330
did not have control over what she said

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.180
to investors about the company,

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.290
over what she said to business partners

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.610
or over what she said to journalists.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:08.880
- [Narrator] Pre-trail court filings

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.970
from Balwani's attorneys

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.340
could also offer insight
into what's to come

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.880
in his criminal trial.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.890
In one November 2021 filing,

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.180
Balwani's defense team
sought to limit evidence

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.170
involving patients, including the results

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.420
of tests that were performed

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.180
using non-Theranos diagnostic equipment.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.370
The judge denied that request.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.510
In order for Balwani to be found guilty,

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.930
the prosecution must prove
beyond a reasonable doubt

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.610
he had the intent to defraud
patients or investors

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:37.000
about the efficacy of Theranos'
blood testing technology.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.850
- So in the case of investors

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.660
that Mr. Balwani told a lie

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.840
that was significant enough
that an investor thought oh,

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:45.790
well, that's great.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.260
I'm going to invest in that company

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.986
and that might have been
a revenue projection

00:05:48.986 --> 00:05:51.580
or a claim about their relationship

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.970
with Walgreens, the pharmacy chain

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.530
that wasn't true but
that was appealing enough

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.816
that it caused an investor
to write them a check.

00:05:58.816 --> 00:06:01.566
(dramatic music)

